# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# frontend/Dockerfile's build context is the PROJECT ROOT (see docker-compose.yml
# -- `context: .`) so it can COPY both frontend/ and nginx/. Without this
# file, `docker build`/`docker compose build` would transmit EVERYTHING in
# the repo root to the Docker daemon as build context -- including a real
# ".env" full of secrets, if one exists on disk, even though no COPY
# instruction ever references it. Excluding it here means it's never even
# sent over, not just "not copied into the final image".
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets -- never send these to the Docker daemon as build context ------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.azure.example
# frontend-app/.env.production holds no secret -- just the same
# same-origin "/api" default already baked into src/lib/api.ts's own
# fallback -- checked in so a plain local `npm run build` (outside
# Docker) matches what frontend/Dockerfile's frontend-app-build stage
# produces.
!frontend-app/.env.production

# --- Git / editors / OS -------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Python (backend has its own Dockerfile/context; nothing here needs these
# but keep the build context lean regardless) ---------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.venv*

# --- Logs / misc ---------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
node_modules/

# --- Frontend test suite -- CI/local-dev only, never shipped ----------------
# frontend/tests/ is its own npm project (jsdom + friends) that exists
# purely for `node --test` (see .github/workflows/ci.yml and
# frontend/tests/package.json). build-frontend/build.js walks EVERY file
# under frontend/ and copies anything that isn't .js/.html straight through
# unmodified -- .test.mjs files don't end in ".js", so without this they'd
# ship into the final image byte-for-byte, publicly served right alongside
# the real app (e.g. /tests/login-form-wiring.test.mjs). Worse,
# frontend/tests/node_modules/** would get walked too and fed to
# terser/javascript-obfuscator as if it were application code, which
# doesn't just bloat the image -- it can outright fail the build (a jsdom
# test fixture under node_modules trips terser with a syntax error).
frontend/tests/

# --- Docs not needed inside the image ------------------------------------------
README.md
